#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-interpret-trailers(1)"
msgstr "git-interpret-trailers(1)"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr "NAME"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:7
msgid ""
"git-interpret-trailers - Add or parse structured information in commit "
"messages"
msgstr ""
"git-interpret-trailers - コミットメッセージの構造化情報を追加またはパースしま"
"す"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr "SYNOPSIS"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:14
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "'git interpret-trailers' [--in-place] [--trim-empty]\n"
#| "\t\t\t[(--trailer <token>[(=|:)<value>])...]\n"
#| "\t\t\t[--parse] [<file>...]\n"
msgid ""
"'git interpret-trailers' [--in-place] [--trim-empty]\n"
"\t\t\t[(--trailer (<key>|<key-alias>)[(=|:)<value>])...]\n"
"\t\t\t[--parse] [<file>...]\n"
msgstr ""
"'git interpret-trailers' [--in-place] [--trim-empty]\n"
"\t\t\t[(--trailer <token>[(=|:)<value>])...]\n"
"\t\t\t[--parse] [<file>...]\n"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "DESCRIPTION"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:20
msgid ""
"Add or parse 'trailer' lines that look similar to RFC 822 e-mail headers, at "
"the end of the otherwise free-form part of a commit message. For example, in "
"the following commit message"
msgstr ""
"コミット メッセージの自由形式部分の最後の、 RFC 822 電子メール・ヘッダーに似"
"た「トレーラー」(trailer)行の追加またはパースを行います。 たとえば、 以下コ"
"ミットメッセージ:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "subject\n"
msgstr "subject\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.\n"
msgstr "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:28
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"
msgstr ""
"Signed-off-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:31
msgid "the last two lines starting with \"Signed-off-by\" are trailers."
msgstr "ここで、「Signed-off-by」で始まる最後の 2 行はトレーラーです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:37
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This command reads commit messages from either the <file> arguments or "
#| "the standard input if no <file> is specified.  If `--parse` is specified, "
#| "the output consists of the parsed trailers.  Otherwise, this command "
#| "applies the arguments passed using the `--trailer` option, if any, to "
#| "each input file. The result is emitted on the standard output."
msgid ""
"This command reads commit messages from either the <file> arguments or the "
"standard input if no <file> is specified.  If `--parse` is specified, the "
"output consists of the parsed trailers coming from the input, without "
"influencing them with any command line options or configuration variables."
msgstr ""
"このコマンドは、 <file> 引数、 または <file> が指定されていない場合は標準入力"
"からコミット・メッセージを読み取ります。 `--parse` が指定されている場合、 出"
"力はパースされたトレーラーで構成されます。 それ以外の場合、 このコマンドは、 "
"`--trailer` オプションを使用して渡された引数(存在する場合)を各入力ファイルに"
"適用します。 結果は標準出力に出力されます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:43
msgid ""
"Otherwise, this command applies `trailer.*` configuration variables (which "
"could potentially add new trailers, as well as reposition them), as well as "
"any command line arguments that can override configuration variables (such "
"as `--trailer=...` which could also add new trailers), to each input file. "
"The result is emitted on the standard output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:50
msgid ""
"This command can also operate on the output of linkgit:git-format-patch[1], "
"which is more elaborate than a plain commit message. Namely, such output "
"includes a commit message (as above), a \"---\" divider line, and a patch "
"part.  For these inputs, the divider and patch parts are not modified by "
"this command and are emitted as is on the output, unless `--no-divider` is "
"specified."
msgstr ""
"このコマンドでは linkgit:git-format-patch[1] の出力を操作することもできま"
"す。 これは、 素のコミット・メッセージよりも複雑です。 つまり、 このような出"
"力には、 (上記のとおりの)コミット・メッセージと `---` 区切り線とパッチ部分が"
"含まれます。 これらの入力の場合 `--no-divider` が指定されない限り、 区切り線"
"以下とパッチ部分はこのコマンドによって変更されず、 そのまま出力されます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:55
msgid ""
"Some configuration variables control the way the `--trailer` arguments are "
"applied to each input and the way any existing trailer in the input is "
"changed. They also make it possible to automatically add some trailers."
msgstr ""
"いくつかの設定変数は `--trailer` 引数が各入力に適用される方法と、 入力内の既"
"存のトレーラーが変更される方法を制御します。 また、 いくつかのトレーラを自動"
"的に追加することもできます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:62
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "By default, a '<token>=<value>' or '<token>:<value>' argument given using "
#| "`--trailer` will be appended after the existing trailers only if the last "
#| "trailer has a different (<token>, <value>) pair (or if there is no "
#| "existing trailer). The <token> and <value> parts will be trimmed to "
#| "remove starting and trailing whitespace, and the resulting trimmed "
#| "<token> and <value> will appear in the output like this:"
msgid ""
"By default, a '<key>=<value>' or '<key>:<value>' argument given using `--"
"trailer` will be appended after the existing trailers only if the last "
"trailer has a different (<key>, <value>) pair (or if there is no existing "
"trailer). The <key> and <value> parts will be trimmed to remove starting and "
"trailing whitespace, and the resulting trimmed <key> and <value> will appear "
"in the output like this:"
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは、 `--trailer` で指定された `<token>=<value>` または `<token>:"
"<value>` 引数は、既存の最後のトレーラーのペア(<token>, <value>)が指定のペア異"
"なる場合(または、既存のに無い場合)にのみ、指定したモノが既存のトレーラーの後"
"に追加されます。 <token>と<value>の部分は、先頭と末尾の空白がトリミングされ、"
"以下のように出力に表示されます:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:65
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "token: value\n"
msgid "key: value\n"
msgstr "token: value\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:69
msgid ""
"This means that the trimmed <key> and <value> will be separated by `': '` "
"(one colon followed by one space)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:75
msgid ""
"For convenience, a <key-alias> can be configured to make using `--trailer` "
"shorter to type on the command line. This can be configured using the "
"'trailer.<key-alias>.key' configuration variable. The <keyAlias> must be a "
"prefix of the full <key> string, although case sensitivity does not matter. "
"For example, if you have"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:78
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "$ git config trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by\"\n"
#| "$ cat msg.txt\n"
#| "subject\n"
msgid "trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by: \"\n"
msgstr ""
"$ git config trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by\"\n"
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:82
msgid ""
"in your configuration, you only need to specify `--trailer=\"sign: foo\"` on "
"the command line instead of `--trailer=\"Signed-off-by: foo\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:87
msgid ""
"By default the new trailer will appear at the end of all the existing "
"trailers. If there is no existing trailer, the new trailer will appear at "
"the end of the input. A blank line will be added before the new trailer if "
"there isn't one already."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは、 すべての既存のトレーラーの末尾の後ろに新しいトレーラーが出力"
"されます。 既存のトレーラーがない場合は、 新しいトレーラーが入力の末尾の後ろ"
"に出力表示されます。 その新しいトレーラーの前にまだ空行がない場合は、 空行が"
"追加されます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:96
msgid ""
"Existing trailers are extracted from the input by looking for a group of one "
"or more lines that (i) is all trailers, or (ii) contains at least one Git-"
"generated or user-configured trailer and consists of at least 25% trailers.  "
"The group must be preceded by one or more empty (or whitespace-only) lines.  "
"The group must either be at the end of the input or be the last non-"
"whitespace lines before a line that starts with '---' (followed by a space "
"or the end of the line)."
msgstr ""
"入力から、 (i) すべてのトレーラーを含むか、 または (ii) 1つ以上の Git 生成ま"
"たはユーザー構成のトレーラーを含む25％以上のトレーラーで構成される、 1行以上"
"のグループから、 既存のトレーラーを探し出して抽出します。 そのグループの前に"
"は、 1行以上の空行(または空白のみの行)が必要です。 そのグループは、 入力の末"
"尾にあるか、 あるいは `---` で始まる行より前の最後の非空白行達である必要があ"
"ります(その後にスペースまたは行の終わりが続きます)。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:103
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "When reading trailers, there can be no whitespace before or inside the "
#| "<token>, but any number of regular space and tab characters are allowed "
#| "between the <token> and the separator. There can be whitespaces before, "
#| "inside or after the <value>. The <value> may be split over multiple lines "
#| "with each subsequent line starting with at least one whitespace, like the "
#| "\"folding\" in RFC 822. Example:"
msgid ""
"When reading trailers, there can be no whitespace before or inside the "
"<key>, but any number of regular space and tab characters are allowed "
"between the <key> and the separator. There can be whitespaces before, inside "
"or after the <value>. The <value> may be split over multiple lines with each "
"subsequent line starting with at least one whitespace, like the \"folding\" "
"in RFC 822. Example:"
msgstr ""
"トレーラーを読み取る場合、 <token> の前または内部に空白(whitespace)を含めるこ"
"とはできませんが、 <token> とセパレーターの間には、 任意の数の通常の空白"
"(space)文字達とタブ文字達を使用できます。 <value> の前または内部または後ろに"
"空白達(whitespaces)を入れることができます。 RFC 822 の「folding」(折り畳み)の"
"ように、 <value> は複数の行に分割され、 後続の各行の先頭は1つ以上の空白"
"(whitespace)で始まります。"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:107
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "token: This is a very long value, with spaces and\n"
#| "  newlines in it.\n"
msgid ""
"key: This is a very long value, with spaces and\n"
"  newlines in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"token: これは非常に長い値であり、\n"
"空白や改行が含まれます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:111
msgid ""
"Note that trailers do not follow (nor are they intended to follow) many of "
"the rules for RFC 822 headers. For example they do not follow the encoding "
"rule."
msgstr ""
"注意: トレーラーはRFC822ヘッダー規則の多くに従うことを意図してませんし、 従わ"
"ないことに注意してください。 たとえば、 それらはエンコーディング規則に従いま"
"せん。"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr "OPTIONS"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:116
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Edit the files in place."
msgid ""
"`--in-place::`\n"
"\tEdit the files in place.\n"
msgstr "その場でファイルを編集します。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:121
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "If the <value> part of any trailer contains only whitespace, the whole trailer will be removed from the output.  This applies to existing trailers as well as new trailers."
msgid ""
"`--trim-empty::`\n"
"\tIf the <value> part of any trailer contains only whitespace,\n"
"\tthe whole trailer will be removed from the output.\n"
"\tThis applies to existing trailers as well as new trailers.\n"
msgstr "トレーラーの <value> 部分に空白(whitespace)のみが含まれている場合、 出力からトレーラー全体が削除されます。 これは、 新しいトレーラーだけでなく、 既存のトレーラーにも適用されます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:126
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Specify a (<token>, <value>) pair that should be applied as a trailer to the inputs. See the description of this command."
msgid ""
"`--trailer`\n"
"\tSpecify a (<key>, <value>) pair that should be applied as a\n"
"\ttrailer to the inputs. See the description of this\n"
"\tcommand.\n"
msgstr "入力のトレーラーとして適用する必要があるペア(<token>、<value>)を指定します。 詳しくはこのコマンドの説明を参照してください。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:137
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Specify where all new trailers will be added.  A setting provided with '--where' overrides all configuration variables and applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--where' or '--no-where'. Possible values are `after`, `before`, `end` or `start`."
msgid ""
"`--where`\n"
"`--no-where::`\n"
"\tSpecify where all new trailers will be added.  A setting\n"
"\tprovided with '--where' overrides the `trailer.where` and any\n"
"\tapplicable `trailer.<keyAlias>.where` configuration variables\n"
"\tand applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of\n"
"\t'--where' or '--no-where'. Upon encountering '--no-where', clear the\n"
"\teffect of any previous use of '--where', such that the relevant configuration\n"
"\tvariables are no longer overridden. Possible placements are `after`,\n"
"\t`before`, `end` or `start`.\n"
msgstr "すべての新しいトレーラーが追加される場所を指定します。 `--where` で指定する設定は、すべての構成変数をオーバーライドし、 `--where` または `--no-where` が次に出現するまですべての `--trailer` オプションに適用されます。 <placement> として可能な値は、 `after` または `before` または `end` または `start` です。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:149
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Specify what action will be performed when there is already at least one trailer with the same <token> in the input.  A setting provided with '--if-exists' overrides all configuration variables and applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--if-exists' or '--no-if-exists'. Possible actions are `addIfDifferent`, `addIfDifferentNeighbor`, `add`, `replace` and `doNothing`."
msgid ""
"`--if-exists`\n"
"`--no-if-exists::`\n"
"\tSpecify what action will be performed when there is already at\n"
"\tleast one trailer with the same <key> in the input.  A setting\n"
"\tprovided with '--if-exists' overrides the `trailer.ifExists` and any\n"
"\tapplicable `trailer.<keyAlias>.ifExists` configuration variables\n"
"\tand applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of\n"
"\t'--if-exists' or '--no-if-exists'. Upon encountering '--no-if-exists, clear the\n"
"\teffect of any previous use of '--if-exists, such that the relevant configuration\n"
"\tvariables are no longer overridden. Possible actions are `addIfDifferent`,\n"
"\t`addIfDifferentNeighbor`, `add`, `replace` and `doNothing`.\n"
msgstr "入力に同一の <token> を持つトレーラーがすでに少なくとも1つある場合に実行される操作を指定します。 `--if-exists` で指定する設定は、 すべての構成変数をオーバーライドし、 `--if-exists` または `--no-if-exists` が次に出現するまですべての `--trailer` オプションに適用されます。 可能な操作は `addIfDifferent`, `addIfDifferentNeighbor`, `add`, `replace`, `doNothing` です。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:161
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Specify what action will be performed when there is no other trailer with the same <token> in the input.  A setting provided with '--if-missing' overrides all configuration variables and applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--if-missing' or '--no-if-missing'. Possible actions are `doNothing` or `add`."
msgid ""
"`--if-missing`\n"
"`--no-if-missing::`\n"
"\tSpecify what action will be performed when there is no other\n"
"\ttrailer with the same <key> in the input.  A setting\n"
"\tprovided with '--if-missing' overrides the `trailer.ifMissing` and any\n"
"\tapplicable `trailer.<keyAlias>.ifMissing` configuration variables\n"
"\tand applies to all '--trailer' options until the next occurrence of\n"
"\t'--if-missing' or '--no-if-missing'. Upon encountering '--no-if-missing,\n"
"\tclear the effect of any previous use of '--if-missing, such that the relevant\n"
"\tconfiguration variables are no longer overridden. Possible actions are `doNothing`\n"
"\tor `add`.\n"
msgstr "入力に同一の <token> を持つ他のトレーラーが無い場合に実行される操作を指定します。 `--if-missing` で指定する設定は、 すべての構成変数をオーバーライドし、 `--if-missing` または `--no-if-missing` が次に出現するまですべての `--trailer` オプションに適用されます。 可能な操作は `doNothing`, `add` です。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:164
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Output only the trailers, not any other parts of the input."
msgid ""
"`--only-trailers::`\n"
"\tOutput only the trailers, not any other parts of the input.\n"
msgstr "トレーラーのみを出力し、入力の他の部分は出力しません。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:169
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Output only trailers that exist in the input; do not add any from the command-line or by following configured `trailer.*` rules."
msgid ""
"`--only-input::`\n"
"\tOutput only trailers that exist in the input; do not add any\n"
"\tfrom the command-line or by applying `trailer.*` configuration\n"
"\tvariables.\n"
msgstr "入力に存在するトレーラーのみを出力します。コマンドラインや、構成された `trailer.*` ルールに従って追加することはありません。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--unfold::`\n"
"\tIf a trailer has a value that runs over multiple lines (aka \"folded\"),\n"
"\treformat the value into a single line.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:180
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--parse::`\n"
"\tA convenience alias for `--only-trailers --only-input\n"
"\t--unfold`. This makes it easier to only see the trailers coming from the\n"
"\tinput without influencing them with any command line options or\n"
"\tconfiguration variables, while also making the output machine-friendly with\n"
"\t--unfold.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:185
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Do not treat `---` as the end of the commit message. Use this when you know your input contains just the commit message itself (and not an email or the output of `git format-patch`)."
msgid ""
"`--no-divider::`\n"
"\tDo not treat `---` as the end of the commit message. Use this\n"
"\twhen you know your input contains just the commit message itself\n"
"\t(and not an email or the output of `git format-patch`).\n"
msgstr "`---` をコミットメッセージの終わりとして扱わないでください。(電子メールや `git format-patch`の出力が含まれておらず、)入力にコミットメッセージ自体だけが含まれていることがわかっている場合にこれを使用します。"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION VARIABLES"
msgstr "CONFIGURATION VARIABLES"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.separators"
msgstr "trailer.separators"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:194
msgid ""
"This option tells which characters are recognized as trailer separators. By "
"default only ':' is recognized as a trailer separator, except that '=' is "
"always accepted on the command line for compatibility with other git "
"commands."
msgstr ""
"このオプションは、どの文字がトレーラー区切り文字として認識されるかを示しま"
"す。 デフォルトでは、 `:` のみがトレーラー区切り文字として認識されます。ただ"
"し、他のgitコマンドとの互換性のために、コマンドラインでは `=` が常に受け入れ"
"られます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:198
msgid ""
"The first character given by this option will be the default character used "
"when another separator is not specified in the config for this trailer."
msgstr ""
